					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Some minor nitpicks/issues I have with the article:</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;minor&nbsp;nitpicks/issues</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;minor&nbsp;nitpicks/issues</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p>For the identifier, I'd suggest being consistent and use either 'Iron-Priest.aic' or 'Artificially Intelligent Mekhanite Priest'. Alternatively you could do something like 'Iron-Priest.aic (Artificially Intelligent Mekhanite Priest internally)' and use 'Artificially Intelligent Mekhanite Priest' whenever it's an internal report and use 'Iron-Priest.aic' whenever it's an external report.</p> <blockquote> <p>To Ms Iris Dark:</p> </blockquote> <p>I'd change 'Ms' to 'Ms.' since there's a period whenever I see 'Miss' abbreviated.</p> <blockquote> <p>Memo XX</p> </blockquote> <p>The last memo is missing the numbers.</p> </div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;minor&nbsp;nitpicks/issues</a></div> </div> </div> 
				 	]]>
